**Memo**  
**To:** Operations Team, GreenWave Utilities  
**From:** Sarah Thompson, Senior Operations Manager  
**Date:** March 15, 2024  
**Subject:** Update on Infrastructure Enhancement and System Integration

As part of our commitment to improving service reliability and operational efficiency, I want to provide an update on our ongoing infrastructure enhancement initiatives and the integration of the new Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) system. Since the initiation of Project Phoenix in January, we have successfully completed the first phase, which involved upgrading our transmission lines across the Riverside District. This upgrade, which included the replacement of 25 miles of aging cables, is expected to reduce outage times by 30% over the next year.

In collaboration with our partners at EcoTech Solutions, we are currently in the process of implementing the SCADA system, which will provide real-time monitoring and control capabilities. This system is crucial for managing our energy distribution and will facilitate better decision-making by our operations team. The integration is scheduled for completion by May 1, 2024, and training sessions will commence the following week. I encourage everyone to participate actively, as understanding this system will be vital for our daily operations.

Additionally, I want to highlight the importance of our relationship with the State Energy Commission. Their recent funding approval of $500,000 for renewable energy projects will significantly bolster our efforts to transition to more sustainable practices. We are currently evaluating how to best allocate these funds to maximize impact, particularly in the development of solar energy farms in the Green Valley region.

As we continue to forge ahead with these initiatives, your cooperation and commitment are crucial. Please ensure that your teams are aligned with these operational changes and feel free to reach out with any questions or suggestions regarding our path forward. Together, we can enhance the reliability of our services and contribute to a more sustainable future for our community.

Thank you for your continued hard work and dedication. 

Best,  
Sarah Thompson  
Senior Operations Manager  
GreenWave Utilities